  caption: [
    Spectral density of scalar induced gravitational waves for $w = 1 / 3$ and constant $c_s$ for a Dirac delta primordial spectrum @eq:pdirac. On the left we fix $k_(upright(p))$ and $A_(cal(R)) = 1$ and vary $c_s^2 = 1 , 1 / 3 , 1 / 9$ respectively in blue, red and orange. We note the resonant peak moves to the left and the amplitude increases while decreasing $c_s$. On the right, we fix $k_(upright("bump"))$ @eq:kbump and require the same amplitude using @eq:bump. Then we fix $A_(cal(R)) = 1$ for $c_s^2 = w$. We note how all the curves share the same IR behavior and that the position of the resonant peak coincides. For $c_s = 1$ the resonant peak lies precisely at the cut-off.
